# RAG Index Progress Patterns

## State Machine Driven

Use state machine for RAG progress in TanaStreamingUpload.tsx and index.ts:

- Single source of truth: Upload state machine controls all RAG-related state
- Derived state: ragLoading and ragError automatically derived from machine state
- Centralized updates: All progress updates go through updateUploadProgress

## SSE Event Processing

Server-Sent Events from preload.py processed with:

- Event validation: validateProgressEvent checks data integrity
- Progress transformation: createProgressUpdate normalizes all event types  
- Phase timing: Automatic tracking of phaseStartTimes and phaseCompletedTimes

## PhaseItem Display Rules

Each PhaseItem.tsx manages its own:

- Status determination, progress calculation, timing
- Visibility (auto-hides deletion phase when not needed)
- Error detection (shows progress bars only for active phases or errors)
- Live updates with own timer for real-time elapsed time

## Progress Display Logic

- Active phases: Show progress bar with percentage and ETA
- Completed phases: Show elapsed time in top-right corner
- Error cases: Show orange progress bar with "(with errors)" text
- Hidden phases: Deletion phase hidden when totalNodesToDelete === 0

## Error Handling

Network error recovery with:

- Categorized errors: Network, timeout, file size, auth, server errors
- Recovery suggestions: Specific guidance for each error type
- Safeguards: Prevent duplicate completion/error transitions

Timeout detection was removed as progress updates are frequent (every second).

## UI State Management

Consolidated state logic in RAGIndex.tsx:

- Single state function: determineUIState centralizes all UI state logic
- Clear states: 'progress' | 'error' | 'loading' | 'ready' | 'empty'
- Switch rendering: Replace complex conditionals with clean switch statements

This ensures consistent, reliable, and maintainable progress reporting.
